from pathlib import Path
import html
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
parts=[]
def para(text):parts.append('<p>'+text+'</p>')
def eq(tex):parts.append('<div class="equation" data-tex="'+html.escape(tex,quote=True)+'"></div>')
def title(text):parts.append('<h2>'+text+'</h2>')
para('For every fixed order, there is an analytical construction valid at every sufficiently large qubit number. It certifies the requested order and failure of the next one. The explicit size condition below is sufficient and conservative; it does not settle existence for every smaller pair.')
eq(r't\ge1,\qquad N\ge4t(t+1)^4\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\exists\,|\psi_{N,t}\rangle\text{ of exactly AC order }t.')
para('All occupied Dicke coefficients are square roots of positive rational numbers. The construction requires one matrix inversion of size t + 1, with no numerical optimization. Support separation and moment matching follow the published approach in <a href="https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.92.052333">Baguette, Damanet, Giraud and Martin (2015), Sections V–VI</a>. The rational grid weights, explicit sufficient bound and next-order coherence proof are derived in this note. No optimality or priority claim is made for the threshold.')
title('Explicit coefficients')
eq(r's=t+1,\quad m=\lfloor N/s\rfloor,\quad R=N-sm,\quad x_i=\frac{si}{N}.')
eq(r'q_i=\begin{cases}\dfrac{s}{N+1},&0\le i<m,\\[4pt]\dfrac{R+1}{N+1},&i=m.\end{cases}')
eq(r'v(x)=(1,x,\ldots,x^t)^T,\quad G=\sum_{i=0}^m q_i v(x_i)v(x_i)^T,\quad\mu=\frac1{N+1}\sum_{r=0}^N v(r/N).')
eq(r'\boxed{\ w_i=q_i v(x_i)^TG^{-1}\mu,\qquad |\psi_{N,t}\rangle=\sum_{i=0}^m\sqrt{w_i}\,|D_N^{(si)}\rangle.\ }')
para('Every entry of G and μ is rational. The matrix G is positive definite once m ≥ t. The bound above guarantees wᵢ &gt; qᵢ/2 for every i. Below that bound the same formula works whenever all its weights are strictly positive.')
title('Why it is t-anticoherent')
eq(r'\sum_iw_i v(x_i)=GG^{-1}\mu=\mu\quad\Longrightarrow\quad\sum_iw_i(si)^a=\frac1{N+1}\sum_{r=0}^Nr^a\quad(0\le a\le t).')
para('The zeroth moment normalizes the state. Occupied excitation indices are separated by t + 1, so every off-diagonal entry of every reduction through order t is zero. Its diagonal entries obey')
eq(r'(\rho_q)_{aa}=\sum_r|c_r|^2\frac{\binom ra\binom{N-r}{q-a}}{\binom Nq}\quad(0\le q\le t).')
para('The factor multiplying |cᵣ|² is a polynomial in r of degree at most q. Moment matching makes it equal to its uniform average over all Dicke indices. Vandermonde’s identity gives 1/(q + 1). Thus every reduction through order t is maximally mixed in its symmetric subspace.')
title('Why the next order fails')
para('At order s = t + 1, adjacent occupied indices can contribute a coherence. Every contribution has a strictly positive real amplitude:')
eq(r'\boxed{\ (\rho_s)_{0s}=\sum_{i=0}^{m-1}\sqrt{w_iw_{i+1}}\,\frac{\binom{N-s}{si}}{\sqrt{\binom N{si}\binom N{s(i+1)}}}>0.\ }')
para('A maximally mixed state has no such off-diagonal entry. This proves exact order t without a numerical tolerance.')
parts.append('<details><summary>Proof that all weights are positive</summary>')
para('The weight formula is invariant under invertible changes of polynomial basis. Use the shifted orthonormal Legendre basis')
eq(r'f_\ell(x)=\sqrt{2\ell+1}\,P_\ell(2x-1),\quad0\le\ell\le t,\qquad\|f\|_\infty\le t+1,\quad\|f^\prime\|_\infty\le t(t+1)^2.')
para('Couple a uniform variable U on [0,1) to Z = floor((N + 1)U)/N, then to X = s floor(NZ/s)/N. Z is uniform on the full Dicke grid and X has probabilities qᵢ. Their distances satisfy')
eq(r'|U-Z|\le\frac1{N+1},\qquad|Z-X|\le\frac tN,\qquad|U-X|\le\frac{t+1}{N}.')
para('With H = E[f(X)f(X)ᵀ] and b = E[f(Z)] − E[f(X)], the derivative bound for ffᵀ yields')
eq(r'\|H-I\|\le\frac{2t(t+1)^4}{N}\le\frac12,\qquad\|b\|\le\frac{t^2(t+1)^2}{N}.')
para('Since f₀ = 1, He₀ = E[f(X)]. Therefore')
eq(r'\frac{w_i}{q_i}=1+f(x_i)^TH^{-1}b\ge1-\frac{2t^2(t+1)^3}{N}\ge1-\frac{t}{2(t+1)}>\frac12.')
parts.append('</details>')
title('A simpler family for exact order two')
para('For every N ≥ 7, put k = floor((N − 1)/2) and take only three occupied Dicke indices:')
eq(r'|\psi_N\rangle=\sqrt{p_0}|D_N^{(0)}\rangle+\sqrt{p_k}|D_N^{(k)}\rangle+\sqrt{p_N}|D_N^{(N)}\rangle,')
eq(r'p_0=\frac{3k-N+1}{6k},\qquad p_k=\frac{N(N-1)}{6k(N-k)},\qquad p_N=\frac{2N+1-3k}{6(N-k)}.')
para('All weights are positive, sum to one, and match the first two uniform Dicke moments. Both support gaps are at least three. The third moment has a strictly nonzero deviation:')
eq(r'\sum_r p_r r^3-\frac{N^2(N+1)}4=\frac{N(N-1)(N-2k)}{12}>0.')
para('This proves exact order two for every N ≥ 7. At N = 6 the existing three-component example has a nonzero third-order coherence. For order one, GHZ states work for every N ≥ 2.')
parts.append('<div class="downloads"><a href="proof.tex">Full LaTeX proof ↓</a><a href="construction.py">Analytical construction ↓</a><a href="verify.py">Independent checks ↓</a><a href="verification.json">Verification report ↓</a></div>')
para('Verification reconstructs full reduced states in eight finite examples through t = 6, checks exact moment matching and positivity in the Bernstein basis at the theorem threshold for t = 1,…,8, and verifies the three-component order-two identities symbolically in N and k. These calculations check the formulas; the argument above proves the theorem for all stated N and t.')
(p/'index.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>A general construction of exactly anticoherent states</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><script src="../page.js" defer></script><style>main{max-width:1000px;padding-block:38px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px)}h2{margin:32px 0 16px}.equation{overflow-x:auto;padding:15px 0}details{padding:18px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}.downloads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px;margin-block:25px}</style></head><body><main><a href="../index.html">← Exact-order constructions</a><p class="eyebrow">General analytical family · 5 November 2026</p><h1>Exactly t-anticoherent states for every sufficiently large N</h1>'''+''.join(parts)+'''</main></body></html>''')
